### ============================================================
### End-to-end Checkout Smoke Test — UC-STR-CHK
### ============================================================
### Exercises the full storefront checkout flow:
###   Login → Create Cart → Add Item → Update Checkout (Address)
###   → Select Shipping Rate (Delivery) → Create Payment Intent
###   (Payment, stock reserved) → Checkout (Complete) → List Orders
###   → Cancel Order
###
### Prerequisites:
###   - API running via Aspire (dotnet run --project infra/Aspire/AppHost)
###   - {{base_url}} = http://localhost:5000 (or Aspire service URL)
###   - Replace placeholder GUIDs with real catalog/variant IDs
### ============================================================

# --------------------------------------------------
# Variables — set these before running
# --------------------------------------------------
# @name = demo-flow

# @host = http://localhost:5000
# @base_url = http://localhost:5000

# After login, capture the token:
# @token = {{login.response.body.value.accessToken}}

# After create cart, capture the cart ID:
# @cart_id = {{createCart.response.body.value.id}}

# After checkout, capture the order ID:
# @order_id = {{checkout.response.body.value.id}}

# After create payment intent, capture the payment intent ID:
# @payment_intent_id = {{createPaymentIntent.response.body.value.id}}

# Placeholder IDs — replace with real catalog data
# @variant_id = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
# @shipping_method_id = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002
# @address_id = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003
# @bogus_payment_method_id = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004


### ============================================================
### STEP 1 — Login
### ============================================================
### Authenticate and obtain a Bearer token.
### The token is used by all subsequent requests.

# @name = login
POST {{base_url}}/api/store/identity/auth/login/password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "credential": "customer@example.com",
  "password": "P@ssw0rd123"
}

### Expected: 200 OK
### Capture: response.body.value.accessToken → {{token}}


### ============================================================
### STEP 2 — Create Cart
### ============================================================
### Creates a new draft cart for the authenticated user.
### If a draft cart already exists, returns the existing one.

# @name = createCart
POST {{base_url}}/api/storefront/cart
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Expected: 201 Created
### Capture: response.body.value.id → {{cart_id}}


### ============================================================
### STEP 3 — Add Item to Cart
### ============================================================
### Adds a product variant to the cart with quantity.
### Replace {{variant_id}} with a real catalog variant ID.

# @name = addItem
POST {{base_url}}/api/storefront/cart/items
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "variantId": "{{variant_id}}",
  "quantity": 2
}

### Expected: 200 OK — cart with line items


### ============================================================
### STEP 4 — Update Checkout (Address State)
### ============================================================
### Sets email, shipping address, and shipping method on the cart.
### This transitions the cart from Cart → Address state.

# @name = updateCheckout
PUT {{base_url}}/api/storefront/cart
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "email": "customer@example.com",
  "shipAddressId": "{{address_id}}",
  "shippingMethodId": "{{shipping_method_id}}"
}

### Expected: 200 OK — cart with Address checkout state


### ============================================================
### STEP 5 — Select Shipping Rate (Delivery State)
### ============================================================
### Selects a specific shipping rate for the order.
### This transitions the cart from Address → Delivery state.

# @name = selectShippingRate
POST {{base_url}}/api/storefront/cart/shipping-rate
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "shippingMethodId": "{{shipping_method_id}}"
}

### Expected: 200 OK — cart with Delivery checkout state


### ============================================================
### STEP 6 — Create Payment Intent (Payment State)
### ============================================================
### Creates a gateway payment intent and reserves stock.
### This transitions the cart from Delivery → Payment state.
### Stock is atomically reserved before the gateway call.
### If the gateway or DB save fails, reservations are released.

# @name = createPaymentIntent
POST {{base_url}}/api/storefront/payment/create-intent
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "orderId": "{{cart_id}}",
  "paymentMethodId": "{{bogus_payment_method_id}}",
  "cardNumber": "4111111111111111",
  "currency": "usd",
  "returnUrl": "https://localhost:5001/checkout/return"
}

### Expected: 200 OK — PaymentCapture with clientSecret
### Capture: response.body.value.id → {{payment_intent_id}}


### ============================================================
### STEP 7 — Checkout (Complete State)
### ============================================================
### Completes the checkout: creates an order from the cart,
### consumes stock reservations, and transitions to Complete.

# @name = checkout
POST {{base_url}}/api/storefront/cart/checkout
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "paymentIntentId": "{{payment_intent_id}}"
}

### Expected: 200 OK — order with Complete status
### Capture: response.body.value.id → {{order_id}}


### ============================================================
### STEP 8 — List Orders
### ============================================================
### Lists the customer's orders including the one just created.

# @name = listOrders
GET {{base_url}}/api/storefront/orders
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Expected: 200 OK — paged list containing the new order


### ============================================================
### STEP 9 — Cancel Order
### ============================================================
### Cancels the order created above.
### Only works if the order is in a cancelable state.

# @name = cancelOrder
PUT {{base_url}}/api/storefront/orders/{{order_id}}/cancel
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Expected: 200 OK — order with Canceled status


### ============================================================
### GUARD TEST — E3: Stock failure before payment
### ============================================================
### Tests that stock reservation failure prevents payment intent creation.
### If a variant is out of stock, CreatePaymentIntent should fail
### before hitting the gateway, and no orphaned payment exists.
###
### The handler reserves stock atomically. If reservation fails
### (e.g. insufficient stock), it returns an error and the gateway
### is never called. If the gateway call itself fails after
### reservation, reservations are released via ReleaseCartStockReservationsCommand.

# @name = guardE3_StockFailure
POST {{base_url}}/api/storefront/payment/create-intent
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "orderId": "{{cart_id}}",
  "paymentMethodId": "{{bogus_payment_method_id}}",
  "cardNumber": "4111111111111111",
  "currency": "usd"
}

### Expected: 4xx error (stock reservation failure or invalid state)
### Guard: No orphaned payment intent should exist in the database
### after this failure. The try/catch + release-command handle cleanup.


### ============================================================
### GUARD TEST — State machine: out-of-order transition rejection
### ============================================================
### Attempts to create a payment intent without completing the
### Delivery step first. The handler validates:
###   cart.State must == "Delivery"
### If not, returns 409 InvalidCheckoutTransition.
###
### This test creates a fresh cart and tries to jump straight
### to payment — should be rejected.

# @name = guardStateMachine_NewCart
POST {{base_url}}/api/storefront/cart
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Expected: 201 — new draft cart

###

# @name = guardStateMachine_AddItem
POST {{base_url}}/api/storefront/cart/items
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "variantId": "{{variant_id}}",
  "quantity": 1
}

### Expected: 200 OK

###

# @name = guardStateMachine_SkipToPayment
POST {{base_url}}/api/storefront/payment/create-intent
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "orderId": "{{guardStateMachine_NewCart.response.body.value.id}}",
  "paymentMethodId": "{{bogus_payment_method_id}}",
  "cardNumber": "4111111111111111",
  "currency": "usd"
}

### Expected: 409 Conflict — InvalidCheckoutTransition
### The cart is still in Cart/Draft state, not Delivery.
### Message: "Cannot transition from {cart.State} to Payment."
